{"content_id":"CL-BPW-C2-001-CUSTODY","domain_id_primary":"D-BKL","domain_ids_secondary":["D-PRP","D-WRD"],"content_type":"claim","route_file":"courses/pathway-backline-props-wardrobe-02-department-systems.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-BPW-SYSTEMS","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"Department Systems","lesson_identifier":"Custody & Ownership","block_identifier":"assigned-custody","question_identifier":"bp2q1","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Assigned custody means responsibility for the defined item/state/work scope that was actually handed over; it does not transfer the department head, artist technician or production owner's broader authority over settings, contents, presets or final decisions.","content_classification":"crew_blueprint_framework","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"system_reasoning","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Work-control framework grounded in field-practice ownership patterns."}
{"content_id":"CL-BPW-C2-002-MOVE-CHANGE","domain_id_primary":"D-BKL","domain_ids_secondary":["D-PRP","D-WRD"],"content_type":"claim","route_file":"courses/pathway-backline-props-wardrobe-02-department-systems.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-BPW-SYSTEMS","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"Department Systems","lesson_identifier":"State Preservation","block_identifier":"move-versus-change","question_identifier":"bp2q2","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Permission to place or move an assigned item does not automatically include permission to alter its settings, contents, preset, packing state or condition; those changes require the responsible department/process to assign them.","content_classification":"crew_blueprint_framework","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"system_reasoning","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Transferable verification heuristic, not a universal ownership law."}
{"content_id":"CL-BPW-C2-003-RECONCILIATION","domain_id_primary":"D-BKL","domain_ids_secondary":["D-PRP","D-WRD","D-LOG"],"content_type":"claim","route_file":"courses/pathway-backline-props-wardrobe-02-department-systems.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-BPW-SYSTEMS","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"Department Systems","lesson_identifier":"Strike & Returns","block_identifier":"reconcile-state","question_identifier":"bp2q3","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"For department-owned show assets, physical removal from stage is not necessarily the end of the work package; the responsible workflow can include reconciling expected items, actual items, location/packing state and observed condition before handoff is complete.","content_classification":"cross_source_pattern","safety_criticality":"low","authority_implication":"system_reasoning","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Exact inventory, condition and signoff procedure remains department/show/shop specific."}
{"content_id":"CL-BPW-C2-004-DISCREPANCY","domain_id_primary":"D-BKL","domain_ids_secondary":["D-PRP","D-WRD"],"content_type":"boundary","route_file":"courses/pathway-backline-props-wardrobe-02-department-systems.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-BPW-SYSTEMS","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"Department Systems","lesson_identifier":"Discrepancies","block_identifier":"no-silent-substitution","question_identifier":"bp2q4","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"When an expected accessory/item/state is missing or inconsistent, identify and report the discrepancy rather than silently substituting, changing or closing the work package from assumption alone.","content_classification":"crew_blueprint_framework","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"system_reasoning","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Exact escalation path and substitution authority are department-specific."}
{"content_id":"CL-BPW-C2-005-CLOSED-LOOP","domain_id_primary":"D-BKL","domain_ids_secondary":["D-PRP","D-WRD","D-COM"],"content_type":"claim","route_file":"courses/pathway-backline-props-wardrobe-02-department-systems.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-BPW-SYSTEMS","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"Department Systems","lesson_identifier":"Handoff","block_identifier":"closed-loop-report","question_identifier":"bp2q5","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"A useful closed-loop department report identifies the relevant asset/work package, its location or observed state, what was actually observed/done, any unresolved discrepancy, and the specific next question or handoff rather than implying unverified completion.","content_classification":"crew_blueprint_framework","safety_criticality":"low","authority_implication":"system_reasoning","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Crew Blueprint communication framework; exact vocabulary and reporting channel vary."}
{"content_id":"Q-BPW-C2-BP2Q1","domain_id_primary":"D-BKL","domain_ids_secondary":["D-PRP","D-WRD"],"content_type":"question","route_file":"courses/pathway-backline-props-wardrobe-02-department-systems.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-BPW-SYSTEMS","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"Department Systems","lesson_identifier":"Knowledge Check","block_identifier":"bp2q1","question_identifier":"bp2q1","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"What does assigned custody of a department item mean?","content_classification":"assessment_prompt","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"system_reasoning","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Existing scored BPW C2 question normalized."}
{"content_id":"QR-Q-BPW-C2-BP2Q1","domain_id_primary":"D-BKL","domain_ids_secondary":["D-PRP","D-WRD"],"content_type":"answer_rationale","route_file":"courses/pathway-backline-props-wardrobe-02-department-systems.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-BPW-SYSTEMS","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"Department Systems","lesson_identifier":"Knowledge Check","block_identifier":"bp2q1-rationale","question_identifier":"bp2q1","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"It means responsibility for the defined scope that was actually handed over; broader department authority, settings, contents and final decisions remain with the responsible department/process unless separately assigned.","content_classification":"crew_blueprint_framework","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"system_reasoning","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Derived from CL-BPW-C2-001-CUSTODY."}
{"content_id":"Q-BPW-C2-BP2Q2","domain_id_primary":"D-BKL","domain_ids_secondary":["D-PRP","D-WRD"],"content_type":"question","route_file":"courses/pathway-backline-props-wardrobe-02-department-systems.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-BPW-SYSTEMS","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"Department Systems","lesson_identifier":"Knowledge Check","block_identifier":"bp2q2","question_identifier":"bp2q2","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"You've been assigned to place a performer's amp. Does that also authorize changing its settings?","content_classification":"assessment_prompt","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"system_reasoning","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Existing scored BPW C2 question."}
{"content_id":"QR-Q-BPW-C2-BP2Q2","domain_id_primary":"D-BKL","domain_ids_secondary":["D-PRP","D-WRD"],"content_type":"answer_rationale","route_file":"courses/pathway-backline-props-wardrobe-02-department-systems.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-BPW-SYSTEMS","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"Department Systems","lesson_identifier":"Knowledge Check","block_identifier":"bp2q2-rationale","question_identifier":"bp2q2","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"No. Placement/movement and changing a device's settings are separate authority decisions; configuration remains with the responsible department or artist technician unless explicitly reassigned.","content_classification":"crew_blueprint_framework","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"system_reasoning","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Derived from CL-BPW-C2-002-MOVE-CHANGE."}
{"content_id":"Q-BPW-C2-BP2Q3","domain_id_primary":"D-BKL","domain_ids_secondary":["D-PRP","D-WRD","D-LOG"],"content_type":"question","route_file":"courses/pathway-backline-props-wardrobe-02-department-systems.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-BPW-SYSTEMS","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"Department Systems","lesson_identifier":"Knowledge Check","block_identifier":"bp2q3","question_identifier":"bp2q3","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Is strike complete as soon as the department item is offstage?","content_classification":"assessment_prompt","safety_criticality":"low","authority_implication":"system_reasoning","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Existing scored BPW C2 question normalized."}
{"content_id":"QR-Q-BPW-C2-BP2Q3","domain_id_primary":"D-BKL","domain_ids_secondary":["D-PRP","D-WRD","D-LOG"],"content_type":"answer_rationale","route_file":"courses/pathway-backline-props-wardrobe-02-department-systems.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-BPW-SYSTEMS","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"Department Systems","lesson_identifier":"Knowledge Check","block_identifier":"bp2q3-rationale","question_identifier":"bp2q3","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Not necessarily. The assigned workflow may still require reconciliation of expected versus actual items, location/packing state and observed condition before the responsible department considers the handoff complete.","content_classification":"cross_source_pattern","safety_criticality":"low","authority_implication":"system_reasoning","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Derived from CL-BPW-C2-003-RECONCILIATION."}
{"content_id":"Q-BPW-C2-BP2Q4","domain_id_primary":"D-BKL","domain_ids_secondary":["D-PRP","D-WRD"],"content_type":"question","route_file":"courses/pathway-backline-props-wardrobe-02-department-systems.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-BPW-SYSTEMS","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"Department Systems","lesson_identifier":"Knowledge Check","block_identifier":"bp2q4","question_identifier":"bp2q4","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"An expected accessory is missing during reconciliation. What should you do?","content_classification":"assessment_prompt","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"system_reasoning","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Existing scored BPW C2 question."}
{"content_id":"QR-Q-BPW-C2-BP2Q4","domain_id_primary":"D-BKL","domain_ids_secondary":["D-PRP","D-WRD"],"content_type":"answer_rationale","route_file":"courses/pathway-backline-props-wardrobe-02-department-systems.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-BPW-SYSTEMS","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"Department Systems","lesson_identifier":"Knowledge Check","block_identifier":"bp2q4-rationale","question_identifier":"bp2q4","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Identify and report the discrepancy through the responsible department process. Do not silently substitute an item, alter the expected state or close the package based on assumption alone.","content_classification":"crew_blueprint_framework","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"system_reasoning","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Derived from CL-BPW-C2-004-DISCREPANCY."}
{"content_id":"Q-BPW-C2-BP2Q5","domain_id_primary":"D-BKL","domain_ids_secondary":["D-PRP","D-WRD","D-COM"],"content_type":"question","route_file":"courses/pathway-backline-props-wardrobe-02-department-systems.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-BPW-SYSTEMS","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"Department Systems","lesson_identifier":"Knowledge Check","block_identifier":"bp2q5","question_identifier":"bp2q5","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"What makes a useful closed-loop status report for a department-owned item/work package?","content_classification":"assessment_prompt","safety_criticality":"low","authority_implication":"system_reasoning","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Existing scored BPW C2 question normalized."}
{"content_id":"QR-Q-BPW-C2-BP2Q5","domain_id_primary":"D-BKL","domain_ids_secondary":["D-PRP","D-WRD","D-COM"],"content_type":"answer_rationale","route_file":"courses/pathway-backline-props-wardrobe-02-department-systems.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-BPW-SYSTEMS","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"Department Systems","lesson_identifier":"Knowledge Check","block_identifier":"bp2q5-rationale","question_identifier":"bp2q5","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Identify the asset/work package, location or observed state, what was actually done/observed, any unresolved discrepancy, and the specific next question or handoff; do not imply facts or completion that were not verified.","content_classification":"crew_blueprint_framework","safety_criticality":"low","authority_implication":"system_reasoning","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Derived from CL-BPW-C2-005-CLOSED-LOOP."}